@*
    Scene labels: the numbers that float beside the machine.

    THE SPLIT THAT MAKES THIS WORK. Blazor renders the text; JavaScript renders the POSITION.
    Neither writes the other's half.

    The React app used drei's <Html> to put a ValueReadout at a 3D point, deliberately, so that
    the number beside the roll bite is produced by the SAME component as the number in the KPI bar.
    That property is worth keeping, and this is how it survives without drei: each label carries a
    data-anchor, the twin's projector converts the anchor's 3D position to a screen transform every
    frame, and the ValueReadout inside re-renders on its own schedule.

    NOTE THE ABSENCE OF ANY style ATTRIBUTE BELOW, and do not add one. Blazor's DOM diff only
    patches attributes it rendered; because it never renders style, the inline transform set by
    JavaScript is invisible to the diff and survives every re-render of the value inside. Adding
    style="@something" here would make Blazor start owning the attribute and the labels would
    snap back to the top-left corner on every tick.
*@
@using Crm04.Web.Components.Common

<div class="twin-label" data-anchor="STAND">
    <div class="label-chip">
        <span class="label-title">ROLL FORCE</span>
        <ValueReadout TagName="ROLL.FORCE.ACTUAL" Size="sm" />
    </div>
</div>

@* ENTRY and EXIT are LOGICAL ends, not fixed sides. The projector reads the rolling direction
   and swaps their anchors on a reversal, exactly when the strip changes direction (§1). *@
<div class="twin-label" data-anchor="ENTRY">
    <div class="label-chip label-entry">
        <span class="label-title">ENTRY</span>
        <ValueReadout TagName="STRIP.THICKNESS.ENTRY" Size="sm" />
        <ValueReadout TagName="TENSION.ENTRY" Size="sm" />
    </div>
</div>

<div class="twin-label" data-anchor="EXIT">
    <div class="label-chip label-exit">
        <span class="label-title">EXIT</span>
        <ValueReadout TagName="STRIP.THICKNESS" Size="sm" />
        <ValueReadout TagName="TENSION.EXIT" Size="sm" />
    </div>
</div>

<div class="twin-label" data-anchor="DTR">
    <div class="label-chip">
        <span class="label-title">DTR</span>
        <ValueReadout TagName="DTR.DIAMETER" Size="sm" HideBadge="true" />
    </div>
</div>

<div class="twin-label" data-anchor="ETR">
    <div class="label-chip">
        <span class="label-title">ETR</span>
        <ValueReadout TagName="ETR.DIAMETER" Size="sm" HideBadge="true" />
    </div>
</div>

<div class="twin-label" data-anchor="POR">
    <div class="label-chip">
        <span class="label-title">POR</span>
        <ValueReadout TagName="POR.DIAMETER" Size="sm" HideBadge="true" />
    </div>
</div>
